# Project Structure
Rule Type: Always

## Directory Structure
```
src/
├── strategies/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── base.py
│   └── *_strategy.py
├── ibkr/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   └── connection.py
└── utils/
    ├── __init__.py
    ├── data_loader.py
    └── logger.py
```

## Required Files
### Strategies Directory
- `__init__.py`: Package initialization
- `base.py`: Base strategy class
- Strategy files: Must follow pattern `*_strategy.py`
  - Example: `groq_recommendations_strategy.py`

### IBKR Directory
- `__init__.py`: Package initialization
- `connection.py`: IBKR connection management

### Utils Directory
- `__init__.py`: Package initialization
- `data_loader.py`: Data loading utilities
- `logger.py`: Logging configuration

## File Organization Rules
- Each strategy must be in its own file
- Strategy files must inherit from base strategy class
- Connection management must be isolated in ibkr directory
- Utility functions must be in appropriate utility modules
- Configuration files must be in config directory
- Test files must mirror source directory structure

## Module Dependencies
- Strategies can depend on:
  - Base strategy class
  - IBKR connection
  - Utility modules
- IBKR connection can depend on:
  - Utility modules
- Utils can only depend on:
  - Standard library
  - Third-party packages

## Import Structure
- Use absolute imports for all local modules
- Avoid circular dependencies
- Keep dependencies explicit
- Use __init__.py to expose public APIs

## Configuration
- Environment variables in .env file
- Trading parameters in config files
- Logging configuration in logger.py
- Strategy parameters in strategy classes

## Documentation
- README.md in root directory
- API documentation in docstrings
- Strategy documentation in strategy files
- Configuration guide in docs directory
